#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:9
msgid ""
"LUMOS starts from scratch. The requirements "
"(`docs/specs/cahier_des_charges.md`, decisions D1–D13) fix the main "
"orientations; this ADR records the concrete tooling chosen in phase 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:12
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Topic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Choice"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Distribution / import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "`lumos-maxima` on PyPI (`lumos` is taken), `import lumos`, CLI `lumos`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Python versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid ""
"SPEC 0 policy. On 2026-10-16 the latest NumPy (2.5), SciPy (1.18) and JAX"
" (0.11) all require Python ≥ 3.12, so `requires-python = \">=3.12\"`; CI "
"tests 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Build backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "`hatchling` with `hatch-vcs` (version derived from git tags)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "`src/` layout, typed package (`py.typed`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Lint / format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "`ruff` (lint and format), configured in `pyproject.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Type checking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid ""
"`pyright` in standard mode; annotations of public code enforced by ruff "
"(`ANN` rules) in `src/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid ""
"`pytest`, `pytest-cov`, `hypothesis`; markers `network`, `hardware`, "
"`gpu`, `slow` excluded by default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Test discipline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid ""
"tests first, separate test commits, independent reference values, "
"enforced by `tools/check_test_integrity.py`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Commits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid ""
"Conventional Commits, scope = plan step (`feat(P4.3): …`); breaking test "
"changes use `test(Px.y)!:` with a justification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid ""
"Sphinx, Breeze theme, MyST, myst-nb, Mermaid; English source, French via "
"gettext (`sphinx-intl`); ReadTheDocs (one project per language)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "CI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid ""
"GitHub Actions: lint, type checking, test matrix (Linux, Windows, macOS ×"
" 3.12–3.14), docs (EN and FR, warnings as errors), test integrity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "Release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "PyPI trusted publishing on GitHub Release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "License"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md
msgid "MIT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:30
msgid "`vfscitools` dependency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:32
msgid ""
"`vfscitools` (archives and `.plt` figures, REQ-RES-*) is **not published "
"on PyPI**, and a package published on PyPI cannot depend on a git URL. It"
" is therefore not declared yet. It must be published on PyPI before step "
"P7.3, when LUMOS starts using it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:36
msgid "Amendment (2026-10-16, step P1.1): no pyright strict mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:38
msgid ""
"Strict mode was tried on `lumos.units`: it reported 17 errors, almost all"
" caused by the incomplete typing of astropy (`Quantity.unit` may be "
"`None`, unknown members) and by NumPy dtype unions, not by actual "
"defects. Silencing them would have required casts everywhere in physics "
"code. Pyright stays in standard mode, and ruff enforces type annotations "
"on every public function of `src/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:43
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:45
msgid ""
"**setuptools + setuptools-scm**: equivalent, but more configuration for "
"the same result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:46
msgid ""
"**mypy**: slower, and its NumPy/JAX stub ecosystem is less convenient "
"than pyright's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:47
msgid ""
"**Python ≥ 3.11** for a wider audience: impossible without giving up the "
"latest NumPy, SciPy and JAX releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:49
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:51
msgid ""
"Version numbers come from git tags (`v0.1.0`). Untagged commits get "
"`0.1.devN` versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0001-stack-and-conventions.md:52
msgid "`vfscitools` must be released on PyPI before P7.3."
msgstr ""

